  "notes": "Official Liebherr brochure datasheet (not the full load chart book). 10 of 15 boom lengths selected; omitted: 22.4, 47.6, 54.9, 56.2, 59.2 m. The 250 t rating (3 m, 13.1 m boom) is ONLY over the rear (sub-column '*' on the source page); the 360° values here come from the other 13.1 m sub-column (max 134 t at 3-4 m). Over-rear 13.1 m column not stored. Remark 10: capacities above 134 t / 151 t require additional pulley block/special equipment. Remark 5: hook block/hook weight is part of the load and must be deducted from the tabulated capacities (chartIncludesHookBlock=true means the tabulated value includes hook block weight). Chart header icon shows outriggers without a stated dimension; span taken from dimension drawing p.3 (9308 mm on one side / 9328 mm on the other longitudinally, 8294 mm transverse) - assumed full outrigger base, verify against the load chart book for VarioBase. maxHookHeight_m 108 is the brochure-cover max hoist height (with jib), not telescopic boom only. maxOutriggerForce_t 116 = 1134 kN from p.8 (other listed value 820 kN / 84 t). counterweight_t 88 = max VarioBallast. operatingWeight_t not stated in brochure (on-road axle loads 5 x 12 t with 0 t counterweight, p.10). Some capacities rise slightly with radius at short radii (e.g. 17.4 m boom 3-4.5 m) - this is as printed in the source. Capacities in metric tons; radius from slewing centre; wind 9 m/s basis."
